Given a list and a target, return the indices of two numbers that add up to it. Use a dict from value to index: for each number, check whether its complement was already seen. That is O(n) instead of the O(n^2) double loop.

```python
def two_sum(nums, target):
    seen = {}
    for i, n in enumerate(nums):
        if target - n in seen:
            return [seen[target - n], i]
        seen[n] = i
    return []

