Interpretability means understanding how a model reaches its predictions. Some models are transparent by design (linear models, small trees), while for black boxes you use post-hoc tools: LIME fits a simple local model around one prediction, SHAP assigns each feature a fair contribution score, and attention maps show where a network "looked".

```python
