Define the base case `exp == 0`, then reduce the exponent. Squaring a half-power gives O(log n) calls instead of O(n).

```python
def power(base, exp):
    if exp < 0:
        return 1 / power(base, -exp)
    if exp == 0:
        return 1
    half = power(base, exp // 2)
    return half * half if exp % 2 == 0 else half * half * base

